            <ArticleTitle>Painful papulovesicles produced by the puss caterpillar.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>125-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A residential gardener complained of immediate stinging when a &quot;fuzzy tan caterpillar&quot; fell across his fingers. He presented with painful hemorrhagic papules on the dorsal aspect of his right hand. Lepidopterism from contact with Megalopyge opercularis is described.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
